# Patch:        010-restore-dropped-default-methods
# Phase:        post
# Target:       extraction/P3Monty31/Extraction/Funs.lean
# Hunks:        1
# Class:        restore
# Gap:          docs/extractor-issues.md 2: charon's multi-target mode
#               (`--targets`) forces `--translate-all-methods`, then filters
#               unused methods after the merge, which drops the default-method
#               roots hax adds (`--start-from core::clone::Clone::clone_from`,
#               `core::cmp::PartialEq::ne`). `--targets` is needed because of 1.
# Cost:         none. Each added field is the body of the CoreModels default
#               method it stands for (`clone.Clone.clone_from.default`,
#               `cmp.PartialEq.ne.default`), inlined.
# Upstreamable: yes: charon could keep `--start-from` roots through the
#               multi-target merge, or hax could pass `--target` to charon's
#               cargo (issue 1).
# Drop when:    charon keeps `--start-from` roots through the multi-target
#               merge, or hax can pass `--target` to charon's cargo (then
#               extract.sh can drop `--targets`).
#
# CoreModels' `core.clone.Clone` has a `clone_from` field and
# `core.cmp.PartialEq` has `ne`, neither with a default. A derived
# `Clone`/`PartialEq` never defines them, so aeneas fills them with the trait's
# default method, but only if charon translated it. hax adds the default methods
# as charon roots for exactly this purpose. We extract with
# `--targets thumbv7em-none-eabi`, the only way to reach charon's cargo with a
# target through hax (issue 1), and in that mode charon drops those roots again.
# So every derived impl comes out missing the field, and Lean rejects the
# structure literal.
#
# The alternative, `--translate-all-methods`, translates every method of every
# impl charon enters, which pulls in p3-field's trait hierarchy (issue 9).
# Adding the field by hand is the narrow fix:
#   clone_from := fun _ source => <clone> source        (= clone_from.default)
#   ne := fun self other => do let b ← <eq> self other; ok (b = false)
#                                                       (= ne.default)
# Five derived `Clone` impls (4 in p3-baby-bear, 1 in p3-monty-31) and one
# derived `PartialEq`.
#
--- a/extraction/P3Monty31/Extraction/Funs.lean
+++ b/extraction/P3Monty31/Extraction/Funs.lean
@@ -215,6 +215,8 @@
   := {
   clone := monty_31.MontyField31.Insts.CoreCloneClone.clone corecloneCloneInst
     data_traitsMontyParametersInst
+  -- PATCHED: default method, body of `core.clone.Clone.clone_from.default`
+  clone_from := fun _ source => (monty_31.MontyField31.Insts.CoreCloneClone.clone corecloneCloneInst data_traitsMontyParametersInst) source
 }
 
 /-- [p3_monty_31::monty_31::{p3_monty_31::monty_31::MontyField31<MP>[TraitClause0]}::new_monty]:
